From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nomorecoolnicknames <nomorecoolnicknames@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:46:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] PhoneSwitcher: notify factories when only the phone->subId
 mapping changes

With the legacy setDataAllowed path (HAL_COMMAND_ALLOW_DATA) the network
factories re-check their requests only on mActivePhoneRegistrants, which
fires from onDdsSwitchResponse, i.e. after a RIL command. When the SIM
loads after radio on, phone 0 is already active and only its subId goes
from -1 to a valid one, so no command is sent and no notification
follows. Every request that reached TelephonyNetworkFactory while the
subId was invalid (shouldApplyNetworkRequest returns false then) stays
"not applied" until the next real switch.

On the Meizu MX6, 22 hours after boot, the mobile-data-always-on
BACKGROUND_REQUEST was still UNSATISFIED and "not applied" in
TelephonyNetworkFactory-0. The data call that later requests brought up
had no request left once Wi-Fi validated, was lost (LOST_CONNECTION) and
was never set up again.

If the evaluation changed the mapping but not the active set, there is
no command in flight to wait for, so notify the registrants right away.
TelephonyNetworkFactory.onActivePhoneSwitch then applies or releases
each request by shouldApplyNetworkRequest, and changes nothing that is
already right.

Change-Id: I389216a129fbe3fb055406e1298f45a02bad912c

diff --git a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/data/PhoneSwitcher.java b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/data/PhoneSwitcher.java
index 411186c..aa5e92f 100644
--- a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/data/PhoneSwitcher.java
+++ b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/data/PhoneSwitcher.java
@@ -1074,6 +1074,7 @@ public class PhoneSwitcher extends Handler {
         boolean hasAnyActiveSubscription = false;
 
         // Check if phoneId to subId mapping is changed.
+        boolean phoneSubChanged = false;
         for (int i = 0; i < mActiveModemCount; i++) {
             int sub = mSubscriptionController.getSubIdUsingPhoneId(i);
 
@@ -1084,6 +1085,7 @@ public class PhoneSwitcher extends Handler {
                 sb.append("->").append(sub);
                 mPhoneSubscriptions[i] = sub;
                 diffDetected = true;
+                phoneSubChanged = true;
             }
         }
 
@@ -1184,16 +1186,32 @@ public class PhoneSwitcher extends Handler {
                     for (Integer i : newActivePhones) log("  " + i);
                 }
 
+                boolean activeSetChanged = false;
                 for (int phoneId = 0; phoneId < mActiveModemCount; phoneId++) {
                     if (!newActivePhones.contains(phoneId)) {
+                        activeSetChanged |= mPhoneStates[phoneId].active;
                         deactivate(phoneId);
                     }
                 }
 
                 // only activate phones up to the limit
                 for (int phoneId : newActivePhones) {
+                    activeSetChanged |= !mPhoneStates[phoneId].active;
                     activate(phoneId);
                 }
+
+                // Legacy IRadio (setDataAllowed): the network factories re-check
+                // their requests only on mActivePhoneRegistrants, which fires from
+                // onDdsSwitchResponse, i.e. only after a RIL command. When the SIM loads
+                // after radio on, the phone is already active and only its subId changes
+                // (-1 -> valid), so no command is sent and every request that arrived while
+                // the subId was invalid stays "not applied" in TelephonyNetworkFactory for
+                // good -- the mobile-data-always-on background request included. With
+                // no command in flight there is nothing to wait for: tell them now.
+                if (phoneSubChanged && !activeSetChanged) {
+                    log("phone->subId mapping changed without a switch, notify active phones");
+                    mActivePhoneRegistrants.notifyRegistrants();
+                }
             }
         }
         return diffDetected;
